{"type":"assistant","uuid":"d3ec6975-6626-478e-b817-a828dcc07675","session_id":"f95bf83c-5848-4ee0-93b6-6e11b8519b95","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"d3ec6975-6626-478e-b817-a828dcc07675","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\n## Summary\n\n### Root Cause\nThe crash occurred in `ESPFragment.java` at line 101 in `ESPTask.doInBackground()`. The code constructed a URL directly from user input without validation:\n\n```java\n.url(\"http://\" + espIPAddress)  // user enters \".lo\" → \"http://.lo\" → crashes\n```\n\nWhen an invalid host like `.lo` is entered, OkHttp's `HttpUrl.get()` throws an `IllegalArgumentException`. This exception was **not** caught by the existing `catch (IOException e)` block (since `IllegalArgumentException` is not a subclass of `IOException`), causing the AsyncTask to crash.\n\n### Fix Applied (3 changes)\n\n1. **Added imports** — `java.net.InetAddress` and `java.net.UnknownHostException`\n\n2. **Host validation in `doInBackground()`** — Before constructing the URL, `InetAddress.getByName(espIPAddress)` validates the host. If invalid, returns `\"INVALID_HOST\"` instead of crashing.\n\n3. **Updated `onPostExecute()`** — Handles the `\"INVALID_HOST\"` sentinel value by showing the same error message (the app already has `R.string.incorrect_IP_address_message` for this purpose).\n\n### Patch File\nThe patch is saved at `/tmp/ESPFragment_fix.patch`."}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":36914,"output_tokens":285,"cache_read_input_tokens":35632,"total_tokens":37199}}}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","uuid":"16518c7d-4f0a-4760-9ea7-2516485aa351","session_id":"f95bf83c-5848-4ee0-93b6-6e11b8519b95","is_error":false,"duration_ms":98744,"duration_api_ms":66439,"num_turns":37,"result":"\n\n## Summary\n\n### Root Cause\nThe crash occurred in `ESPFragment.java` at line 101 in `ESPTask.doInBackground()`. The code constructed a URL directly from user input without validation:\n\n```java\n.url(\"http://\" + espIPAddress)  // user enters \".lo\" → \"http://.lo\" → crashes\n```\n\nWhen an invalid host like `.lo` is entered, OkHttp's `HttpUrl.get()` throws an `IllegalArgumentException`. This exception was **not** caught by the existing `catch (IOException e)` block (since `IllegalArgumentException` is not a subclass of `IOException`), causing the AsyncTask to crash.\n\n### Fix Applied (3 changes)\n\n1. **Added imports** — `java.net.InetAddress` and `java.net.UnknownHostException`\n\n2. **Host validation in `doInBackground()`** — Before constructing the URL, `InetAddress.getByName(espIPAddress)` validates the host. If invalid, returns `\"INVALID_HOST\"` instead of crashing.\n\n3. **Updated `onPostExecute()`** — Handles the `\"INVALID_HOST\"` sentinel value by showing the same error message (the app already has `R.string.incorrect_IP_address_message` for this purpose).\n\n### Patch File\nThe patch is saved at `/tmp/ESPFragment_fix.patch`.","usage":{"input_tokens":1071511,"output_tokens":9839,"cache_read_input_tokens":989312,"total_tokens":1081350},"permission_denials":[]}
